            which nevertheless describe experimentally distinguishable electromagnetic field configurations. (Distinguishable by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aharonov-Bohm+effect"} Aharonov-Bohm effect
            and also to some extent by
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            %em
              %a{:href => "#CirclePrincipalConnections"} Circle-principal connections
            below.)
          %p
            However, not all different gauge potentials describe different physics. The actual configuration space of electromagnetism on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is finer than
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Omega}^2_{cl}(X)
            but coarser than
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Omega}^1(X)
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"} smooth groupoid
          %p
            one finds that two electromagnetic potentials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, A' \in \Omega^1(\mathbb{R}^4)
            for which there is a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^4)
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A' = A + \mathbf{d}\lambda
          %p
            represent
            %em
              different but
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            field configurations. One says that
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                induces a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \colon A \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} A'
            to reflect this.
          %p So the configuration space of electromagnetism does not just have points and coordinate systems. But it is also equipped with the information of a space of gauge transformations between any two coordinate systems laid out in it (which may be empty).
          %p
            To see what the structure of such a
            %em smooth gauge groupoid
            should be, notice that the above defines an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of smooth functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            on smooth
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          #ActionOfFunctionsOnForms.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_{vert}(X \times U)
              for the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-forms"} differential 1-forms
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times U
              with no components along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X \times U , U(1))
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
              valued
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of this group on the 1-forms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho_U
                    \\colon
                    \\Omega^1_{vert}(X \times U) \times C^\infty(X \times U, U(1))
                    \\to
                    \\Omega^1_{vert}(X \times U)
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi d
                      %mi X
                    %mi λ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho_U \colon (A,\lambda) \mapsto A + \mathbf{d}_X \lambda
                    \\,.
          %p
            Given such an action of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_{vert}(X\times U)/C^\infty(X \times U, U(1))
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            a gauge transformation from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \colon A_1 \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} A_2
          #EMGaugeGroupoidOverU.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo =
                          %mi ρ
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^1_{vert}(X\times U)//  C^\infty(X \times U, U(1))
                    \\coloneqq
                    (
                    \\Omega^1_{vert}(X\times U) \times C^\infty(X \times U, U(1))
                    \\stackrel{\overset{t = \rho}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{s = p_1}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\Omega^1_{vert}(X\times U)
                    )
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  = succeed "-parameterized" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∈
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi vert
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1_{vert}(X \times U)
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  are pairs
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi λ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\lambda)
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  an object and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi λ
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in C^\infty(X \times U, U(1))
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi d
                            %mi X
                          %mi λ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A + \mathbf{d}_X \lambda
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  is given by multiplication of the
                  = succeed "-labels" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi λ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X \times U, U(1))
          %p
            This is the discrete
            %em gauge groupoid
            for
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ≔
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0 \coloneqq 0 \in \Omega^1_{vert}(X \times U)
              be the trivial gauge field. Then its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              in the gauge groupoid of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EMGaugeGroupoidOverU"}
              is the group of
              = succeed "-group" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_1(\Omega^1_{vert}(X\times U)// C^\infty(X \times U, U(1)), A_0)
                    \=
                    Aut(A_0)
                    \\simeq
                    C^\infty(U,U(1))
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By definition, an automorphism of
