          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Despite the size of the diagrams in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomGroupoidsOfPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by abstract coordinate charts to probes of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              by these charts, and take gauge transformations between these to gauge transformations between those, in a way that it compatible with changing probes along smooth maps.
          %p
            The following is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            in this context, and it says that this intuition in remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaIntuition"}
            is fully correct:
          #YonedaForPreSmoothGroupoids.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              defines a pre-smooth groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %munder
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo ̲
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{\mathbb{R}}^n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PreSmoothGroupoid"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %munder
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ̲
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underline{\mathbb{R}}^n \colon \mathbb{R}^k  \mapsto C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^k, \mathbb{R}^n)
                    \\in
                    Set
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Grpd
            %p
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              on the right is regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              with only
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              morphisms. This construction constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ̲
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underline{(-)}
                    \\colon
                    CartSp \hookrightarrow PreSmooth1Type
            %p
              making
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of that of pre-smooth groupoids (the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in PreSmooth1Type
              and any Cartesian space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} natural equivalence
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %munder
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ̲
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PreSmooth1Type(\underline{\mathbb{R}}^n, X)
                    \\simeq
                    X(\mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              proper).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              The last statement of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              expresses just the intuition of remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaIntuition"}
              and justifies removing the quotation marks displayed there. It also justifies dropping the extra underline denoting the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              with the pre-smooth groupoid that it represents.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
              (e.g. a
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \colon CartSp^{op} \to Set
            %p then its embedding into groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \colon CartSp^{op} \to Set \hookrightarrow Grpd
            %p is a pre-smooth groupoid.
          %p More generally:
          #ExternalYonedaEmbeddingsIntoPreSmooth1Type.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi t
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mi i
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 0
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{G}_\bullet
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\mathcal{G}_1
                    \\stackrel{\overset{s}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{t}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    \\mathcal{G}_0
                    \\right\}
            %p
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_0, \mathcal{G}_1 \in Smooth0Type
              of smooth sets, equipped with source, target, identity homomorphisms of smooth sets between them, and equipped with a compatibly unital, associative and invertible composition map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 1
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 0
                        %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_1 \underset{\times}{\mathcal{G}_0} \mathcal{G}_1 \to \mathcal{G}_1
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 0
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{G}(\mathbb{R}^n)_\bullet
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\mathcal{G}(\mathbb{R}^n)_1
                    \\stackrel{\overset{s(\mathbb{R}^n)}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i(\mathbb{R}^n)}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{t(\mathbb{R}^n)}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    \\mathcal{G}(\mathbb{R}^n)_0
                    \\right\}
            %p
              is a bare
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n
                    \\mapsto
                    \\mathcal{G}(\mathbb{R}^n)_\bullet
                    \\,.
            %p
              This exhibits sequence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              inclusions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi LieGrpd
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi DiffGrpd
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Grp
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    LieGrpd
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    DiffGrpd
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Grpd(Smooth0Type)
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    PreSmooth1Type
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoids"} internal groupoids
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
              into pre-smooth groupoids, and hence (by further restriction) also of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groupoids"} diffeological groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
              and of course of just bare
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %p
              Regarding a bare groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
              as a pre-smooth groupoid this way means to regard it as equipped with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object"} discrete
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+presheaf"} constant presheaf
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \mapsto \mathcal{G}_\bullet
            %p
              exhibiting the fact that smooth functions from an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              into a geometrically discrete space are constant on one of the points of this space, a situation which here is only refined by the fact that every morphism in the groupoid thus gives a
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              between the two smooth functions that are constant on the two endpoints of this morphism.
          %p A particular case of this of special importance is this:
          #DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet \in Grpd(Smooth0Type)
              for the Lie groupoid which
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi G
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mi i
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mo *
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    G \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\stackrel{\overset{i}{\longleftarrow}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\ast
                    \\right)
            %p
              whose composition is the product operation in the group (the groupoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExternalYonedaEmbeddingsIntoPreSmooth1Type"}
              has groupoids of probes of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi disc
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n
                    \\mapsto
                    B \left(C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n,G)_{disc}\right)
            %p
              where on the right we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-type"} homotopy 1-type
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              is that of smooth
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
          %p More specifically, the following class of examples plays a special role in the theory, as they encode what it takes for a pre-smooth groupoid to be a genuinely smooth groupoid.
          #GroupoidOfCover.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}_{i \in I}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groupoid"}> diffeological groupoid
              )
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})_\bullet
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  manifold of objects is
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ≔
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})_0 \coloneqq \underset{i \in I}{\coprod} U_i
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                  of all the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charts"} charts
                  of the cover;
              %li
                %p
                  manifold of morphisms is
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≔
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %munder
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})_1 \coloneqq  \underset{i,j \in I}{\coprod}U_i \underset{X}{\times} U_j
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                  of all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
                  of charts.
            %p
              and whose source, target and identity maps are the evident inclusions. There is then a
              %em unique
              composition operation.
            %p
              So a global point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to C(\{U_i\})_\bullet
              may be thought of as a pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i)
              of a point in the manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and a label
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              of a chart
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              that contains it, and there is is precisely one morphism between two such global point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i)\to (y,j)
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              as well as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_j
              contain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi j
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(\{U_i\})_\bullet
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; (x,j)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    (x,i)
                    \&amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp;
                    (x,k)
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Under the embedding of example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExternalYonedaEmbeddingsIntoPreSmooth1Type"}
              there is an evident morphism of pre-smooth groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(\{U_i\})
                    \\longrightarrow
                    X
            %p
              from this Cech groupoid of the cover to the manifold that is being covered. This morphism simply forgets the information of which chart or intersection of charts a point is regarded to be in, and just remembers it as a point of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi x
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ((x,i) \to (x,j))
                    \\mapsto
                    (x \stackrel{id_x}{\to} x)
                    \\,.
          #CechCoyclesAsSmoothMaps.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
              the corresponding Cech groupoid, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidOfCover"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              its groupoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              according to example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid"}
            %p
              Then the hom-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PreSmooth1Type(C(\{U_i\}), \mathbf{B}G)
              of maps from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomGroupoidsOfPreSmoothGroupoids"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycles
                  of degree 1 on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  relative to the cover and with values in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %munder
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g_{i j} \;\colon\; U_i \underset{X}{\times} U_j \longrightarrow G
                %p satisfying on each triple intersection the cocycle condition
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g_{i j} g_{j k} = g_{i k}
              %li
                %p
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coboundaries"} coboundaries
                  between such cocycles
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{g_{i j}\}
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mrow
                              %mi j
                              %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\tilde g_{j k}\}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        h_{i} \colon U_i \longrightarrow G
                %p such that on each intersection of charts
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g_{i j} h_j  = h_i \tilde g_{i j}
                        \\,.
            %p
              In particular the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              of the Hom-groupoid is hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
              itself:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi Cech
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ;
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_0
                    PreSmooth1Type(C(\{U_i\}), \mathbf{B}G)
                    \\simeq
                    H^1_{Cech}(X,\{U_i\}; G)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The components of a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})\longrightarrow \mathbf{B}G
              look as follows
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi j
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi g
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi j
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi x
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi g
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi j
                                        %mi k
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi x
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi g
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi i
                                      %mi k
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; (x,j)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    (x,i) &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; (x,k)
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\mapsto
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \bullet
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{g_{i j}(x)}}\nearrow
                    \&amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{g_{j k}(x)}}
                    \\\
                    \\bullet &amp;&amp;\stackrel{g_{i k}(x)}{\to}&amp;&amp; \bullet
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that evaluating the morphism on the point
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast = \mathbb{R}^0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              of groupoids as shown. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G(\mathbb{R}^0)
              has a single object, there is no choice for this functor on the level of objects. On morphisms it has to send each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i,j)
              in a double intersection of the cover to a group element
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{i j}(x)\in G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ( g_{i j} )_{i,j \in I} \colon \underset{i,j}{\coprod} U_i \underset{X}{\times} U_j \longrightarrow G
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              gives that these must be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              (as discussed at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g_{i j}(x) g_{j k}(x) = g_{i k}(x)
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i,j)
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
              cocycle.
            %p
              Similarly, a homotopy between two such morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \colon g \Rightarrow \tilde g
              is in components a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi h
                                  %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi g
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi i
                                      %mi j
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mover
                                      %mi g
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi i
                                      %mi j
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi h
                                  %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (x,i)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    (x,j)
                    }
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\mapsto
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    \\bullet &amp;\stackrel{h_i(x)}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \bullet
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{g_{i j}(x)}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\tilde g_{i j}(x)}}
                    \\\
                    \\bullet &amp;\underset{h_j(x)}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \bullet
                    }
            %p hence is given by smooth functions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (h_i)_{i \in I} \colon \underset{i}{\coprod} U_i \longrightarrow G
            %p such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h_i(x) \tilde g_{i j}(x) = g_{i j}(x) h_j(x)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is precisely the formula characterizing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h_i)_{i \in I}
              as a Cech
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coboundary"} coboundary
          %p
            More along these lines is at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+principal+bundles"} geometry of physics – principal bundles
          %h4#gluing Gluing
          %p
            The “bootstrap”-definition of pre-smooth groupoids
            %a{:href => "#PreSmoothGroupoids"} above
            works as intended, by prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
            %em gluing
            of probes:
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a pre-smooth groupoid, then given a probe of it of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
            and given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to \mathbb{R}^n\}
            of the probe space by other probe spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \simeq \mathbb{R}^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            from knowing its restrictions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{|U_i}\colon U_i \to X
            to these charts, and the information of how these are identified by gauge transformations on double overlaps.
          %p
            Such a system of local data and of gauge identification on double overlaps is just what maps out of the Cech groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidOfCover"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CechCoyclesAsSmoothMaps"}
            for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid"}
          %p
            In other words, the condition that smooth probes of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by coordinate charts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            glue along covers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to \mathbb{R}^n\}
            of these charts is the condition that the groupoid of smooth maps out of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            itself
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^n \longrightarrow X
          %p is equivalent to the groupoid of maps out of the Cech groupoid of any cover
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C(\{U_i\}) \longrightarrow X
          %p
            and is so via the “restriction” map that takes the former and precomposes it with the canonical map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\}) \to \mathbb{R}^n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C(\{U_i\}) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{R}^n
                  }
                  \\,.
          #DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              A pre-smooth groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PreSmooth
                      %mn 1
                      %mi Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PreSmooth1Type
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PreSmoothGroupoid"}
              %em satisfies descent
              if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              and for all differentiably
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+covers"} good open covers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to \mathbb{R}^n\}
              of the
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(\mathbb{R}^n) \simeq PreSmooth1Type(\mathbb{R}^n, X)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    PreSmooth1Type(C(\{U_i\}),X)
            %p
              given by pre-composition with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\}) \to \mathbb{R}^n
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              The condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              is called the
              = succeed "," do
                %em stack condition
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              “descends” down along the cover projection. So a smooth groupoid is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              condition (see the next example) and hence a more systematic terminology would be to say that such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaf"} 2-sheaf
              or rather a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-sheaf"} (2,1)-sheaf
              (since it takes values in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              as opposed to in more general
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PreSmooth0Type \hookrightarrow PreSmooth1Type
              be a pre-smooth groupoid which is really just a pre-smooth set, hence a presheaf on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              that takes values in groupoids with only identity morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Grp
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \colon CartSp^{op} \longrightarrow Set \hookrightarrow Grp
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a smooth groupoid in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              precisely if it is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              condition.
          #SmoothManifoldsSatisfyDescentAsPreSmoothGroupoids.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              In particular, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SmoothMfd
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SmoothMfd \hookrightarrow PreSmooth0Type \hookrightarrow PreSmooth1Type
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              There is an alternative formulation of the whole theory where instead of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              one uses the site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
              of all
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              is a much stronger condition.
            %p
              For instance the presheaves of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet = (G \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} \ast)
              from example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid"}
              satisfy descent on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SmoothMfd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothMfd
            %p
              The choice of the smaller site is the one that is easier to work with, and therefore we stick with that. In fact, most every example of a pre-smooth groupoid that one runs into satisfies descent on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
          %p For example:
          #bfBGbulletSatisfiesDescent.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet
              of example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid"}
              satisfies descent on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to \mathbb{R}^n\}
              a differentiably good open cover, then by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CechCoyclesAsSmoothMaps"}
              the groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PreSmooth1Type(C(\{U_i\}),(\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet)
              is the groupoid of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech 1-cocycles and coboundaries
              with coeffcients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              relative to the cover. But this is equivalently the groupoid of
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi disc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B (C^\infty(G)_{disc})
                    \\simeq
                    PreSmooth1Type(\mathbb{R}^n, (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    PreSmooth1Type(C(\{U_i\}), (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore this is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective functor
              of groupoids. Moreover, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
              of the trivial
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "-functions," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
              of groupoids. Accordingly it is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
              of groupoids.
          %p
            The same argument however shows that on the larger site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
            this object does not satisfy descent. Put positively, this is the content of prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StackMapsFromXtoDeloopingOfG"}
          %h4#weak_equivalences Weak equivalences
          %p
            While the morphisms of pre-smooth groupoids defined above correctly encode morphisms of smooth structures (by taking smooth probes compatibly to smooth probes), they are not sensitive enough yet to the required concept of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
            = succeed "-wise." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
            around that point.
          #Stalks.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt r \lt 1 \in \mathbb{R}
              let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi D
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \simeq D^n_r \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              that regards the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              as the standard
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disk"} disk
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              around the origin in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PreSmooth1Type
              we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi r
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi D
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (D^n)^* X \coloneqq {\underset{\longrightarrow_r}{\lim}} X(D^n_r) \in Grpd
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              (in the 1-category of groupoids) of the restrictions of its groupoids of plots along the inclusion of these open balls – the
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ⟶
