                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              in the above argument. A detailed discussion of how to find
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              with its group structure and smooth structure from
              = succeed "-paths" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is in (
              %a{:href => "#Crainic"}> Crainic
              ).
          %h4#IntegrationToLineNGroup
            Integrating to line/circle Lie
            = succeed "-groups" do
